<BaseLayout title="Start Here" description="An introduction to WTE Wiki and the WhyTrashEarth network.">
  <article class="content card p-24"><p class="eyebrow">Start here</p><h1>Welcome to WTE Wiki.</h1><p>WTE Wiki is the growing public record for WhyTrashEarth: a place to connect projects, preserve context, and make work easier to understand over time.</p><hr class="hr" /><h2>What you’ll find</h2><p>The <a href="/projects">Projects directory</a> points to active initiatives across the network. <a href="/blog">Updates</a> collects new notes and progress as they are published. The <a href="/about">About page</a> explains the larger approach behind the work.</p><h2>How to use this archive</h2><p>Start with the topic that interests you. Some entries are active public sites; others are early concepts or developing records. This wiki will become more detailed as project histories, research, and documentation are added.</p></article>
